2e:["$","figcaption",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Port Republic: the fight for the Coaling"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Tyler’s right rested on the South Fork and his left on the Coaling. Winder’s early attack across the bottomland failed. Taylor’s Louisiana Brigade moved through the woods and made repeated attacks on the Coaling while Ewell’s men arrived from Cross Keys. The diagram does not claim exact regimental geometry. Terrain, bridge spacing, and routes are schematic and not to scale."}],["$","span",null,{"className":"map-actions","children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"/projects/civil-war-field-companion/images/ep154-port-republic-movements.svg","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":["Open full-size map ",["$","$Ld",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$27:props:children:1:props:children:0:props:children:1:props:children:2:props:children:0:props:children:1:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-arrow-up-right","size":13}]]}],["$","a",null,{"href":"National Park Service Port Republic history, Official Records, and Hotchkiss map; see sources below.","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":["Map source ",["$","$Ld",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$27:props:children:1:props:children:0:props:children:1:props:children:2:props:children:0:props:children:1:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-arrow-up-right","size":13}]]}]]}],"$undefined"]}]
